From: originaxiom <originaxiom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:01:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] THE MOVE OF TWENTY OLD FRONT PAGES INTO ONE FOLDER, WITH ONE
 PAGE THAT SAYS WHERE EACH WENT (cld-advisor, at main's word in M12, outside
 its five packages; the owner approved the move to main on 2026-11-12,
 register row P-825; built on 5c7abd72a with the ten patches of series 4
 applied). WHAT MOVES: the twenty pages of main's list, each a dated account
 of an earlier state or a plan or a protocol that a later page replaces, read
 one by one by main. Each goes into docs/retired/ under its own name, as a
 pure rename: no byte of them is changed. WHAT IS WRITTEN: one page,
 docs/MOVED.md, a table of four columns, where the page was, where it is, what
 it is, and what stands in its place now; the last two are main's words. ONE
 ROW IN ONE KEPT PAGE: the front page's table of what to read leads to it. No
 other page is edited, and no citation is rewritten: 74 times a page cites one
 of the old places, each stands as it was written, and the path checker reads
 it through the table. THE TABLE IS HELD by the gate that reads it, and no
 gate is added: each page it names is a tracked file where the table says;
 every page in the folder has its row; no old place is taken again by a file,
 which would make a citation name two pages; no place stands in it twice, no
 page is said to have moved on, and a row that cannot be read is not passed
 over. A TABLE KEYED BY A FILE FOLLOWS THE PAGE: one entry of the attribution
 baseline is keyed by a page that moves; it is renamed with its page, and the
 rule that no ceiling rises without a recorded act reads a moved page's
 ceiling at the place the page is now, the table being the record of the move.
 No table of the third or the fourth series holds one of the twenty. SAID TO
 MAIN, as it asked: no script, no test and no gate reads one of the twenty at
 this head; one checker names one of them in its docstring and reads none, as
 main found. No generated page changes. The lock:
 tests/test_a_moved_page_is_where_the_table_says.py, eight tests. On the
 commit before, all eight fail, the first because a citation of an old place
 does not resolve and the checker reads no table. Tested against planted
 errors; computed once. 0 of 19.

